  "result": "Fixed. Completion input containing `#` is now split correctly.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex.shlex`, which treats `#` as a comment start by default. Even in whitespace-split mode, an unquoted `#` inside a word made the lexer drop the rest of the line, so `cmd a#b c` completed as if it were `cmd a`.\n\n**Fix:** I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` before splitting, with a short comment explaining why.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `cmd a#b c` \u2192 `['cmd', 'a#b', 'c']`, and `cmd \"a#b\" c` gives the same result.\n- I added `test_split_arg_string_hash` to `tests/test_shell_completion.py`. Two of its four cases fail without the fix and pass with it.\n- `tests/test_shell_completion.py`: 62 passed.\n\nI haven't committed anything, and I didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry. Say if you want either.",
